      "content": "You're right to be cautious, as high salt intake may worsen swelling in some cases. Limiting salt to 5-6 grams per day, as recommended, is a good rule of thumb. Ibuprofen is generally not recommended during the third trimester due to potential risks to the fetus, and it's best to consult your doctor for advice on pain management during this time. The symptoms should stabilize on their own once the third trimester ends, but it's crucial to manage them safely and under medical guidance.",
